<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy — FinBrio"
  description="How FinBrio handles your data: what we collect, why, and the choices you have."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="July 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains what information FinBrio ("we", "us") collects when you
    use the FinBrio mobile app and this website, how we use it, and the choices you have.
    We built FinBrio to be useful without being nosy — we collect the minimum needed to
    run the product, and we do not sell your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>Depending on how you use FinBrio, this may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account information.</strong> If you create an account, we collect the email
      address you sign up with (via Firebase Authentication). No account is required to
      browse live markets.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device &amp; usage data.</strong> A randomly generated device identifier, app
      version, and basic technical data used to deliver content and keep the service
      reliable.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notification tokens.</strong> If you enable push notifications or price
      alerts, we store a push token so we can deliver those alerts to your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Subscription status.</strong> If you purchase a subscription, our payments
      provider (RevenueCat, alongside the Apple App Store or Google Play) processes the
      transaction. We receive your entitlement status, not your card details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Diagnostics.</strong> If enabled, anonymized crash and error reports (via
      Sentry) help us find and fix bugs.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Market data, trade disclosures, and macro indicators shown in FinBrio come from public
    sources and are not personal information about you.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide and maintain the app's features, including alerts and subscriptions.</li>
    <li>To authenticate you and keep your account secure.</li>
    <li>To send notifications you've asked for.</li>
    <li>To diagnose problems, prevent abuse, and improve the product.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
    <li>We do not use your data to build advertising profiles.</li>
    <li>We do not share your data except with the service providers below, or where required by law.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>
    We rely on a small set of trusted providers to operate FinBrio, including Google
    Firebase (authentication, database, notifications), RevenueCat and the Apple/Google app
    stores (subscriptions), and Sentry (diagnostics). Each processes data only to provide
    their service to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account and subscription data for as long as your account is active. You can
    request deletion of your account and associated data at any time (see below).
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the app without an account to minimize what's collected.</li>
    <li>Turn push notifications on or off in your device settings.</li>
    <li>Request access to, or deletion of, your account data by emailing us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
  <p>
    FinBrio is an information and analytics tool. Signals, backtests, and briefings are for
    informational purposes only and are not investment advice. Markets involve risk.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy or your data? Email
    <a href="mailto:contact.finbrio@gmail.com">contact.finbrio@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
